{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9200-1","published":"2026-11-25T18:52:08Z","modified":"2026-11-26T05:13:18.269244087Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2025-1352","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-1376"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-1352","CVE-2025-1376","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-1352","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-1376"],"summary":"elfutils vulnerabilities","details":"It was discovered that elfutils incorrectly handled memory when processing\ncertain malformed DWARF data. If a user or automated system were tricked\ninto running readelf on a specially crafted file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause readelf to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-1352)\n\nIt was discovered that strip from elfutils could be made to dereference\ninvalid memory when processing certain sections without data. If a user or\nautomated system were tricked into running strip on a specially crafted\nfile, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause strip to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2025-1376)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"elfutils","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:22.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/elfutils?arch=source&distro=jammy"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"}]}],"versions":["0.185-1build1","0.185-2","0.186-1","0.186-1build1","0.186-1ubuntu0.1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"No subscription required","binaries":[{"binary_name":"debuginfod","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"elfutils","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"libasm1","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"libdebuginfod-common","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"libdebuginfod1","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"libdw1","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"},{"binary_name":"libelf1","binary_version":"0.186-1ubuntu0.2"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"CVE-2025-1352","severity":[{"score":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L","source":